    "result_text": "All 10 tests pass and the build succeeds. The audit log line confirms the new behavior end-to-end:\n\n```\n{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nNote the member id embeds region code `NSWV2` (the plain region `NSW` + the `V2` tag), while `locality` continues to report the plain `NSW`.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**New \u2014 `util/IdentityVersion.java`**: the single home for the version-2 identity release. Holds `VERSION = 2`, the fixed `TAG` (`\"V2\"`), and the three mixing helpers: `regionCode(plain)` (tags the region embedded in the member id), `plainRegion(code)` (recovers the bare region back), and `tagged(input)` (prefixes the tag into a hash input).\n\n**Identity derivation (every identifier now changes, and no v1 value recurs):**\n- `AssignMemberId` \u2014 passes `IdentityVersion.regionCode(...)` as the member-id region, so `NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`.\n- `HouseholdNormalizer.id` \u2014 hashes `IdentityVersion.tagged(key(...))`.\n- `IdentityKey.of` \u2014 hashes `IdentityVersion.tagged(...)`.\n\n**Keeping the user-facing region plain:**\n- `OwnerMapper.locality` \u2014 un-tags via `IdentityVersion.plainRegion(MemberId.regionOf(...))`, so `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment all recompute from the version-2 member id yet keep reporting the bare region code (`NSW`). `MemberId` itself stays a pure formatter, unaware of versioning.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 new `OwnerIdentity` schema; the `Owner` schema now nests `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` under `identity`, drops them from the top level, and adds a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 new `identity(owner)` builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto` (reusing `IdentityKey.forOwner`), and `apiVersion()` returns `IdentityVersion.VERSION`.\n\n**Audit schema:**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 adds a local `SCHEMA_VERSION = 2` constant, emitted as `schemaVersion` in the JSON. (Left the audit event's own schema version independent of the identity-algorithm constant, since they're conceptually distinct version numbers that merely coincide at 2.)\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are untouched.",
