    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, read from the live OfficeFloor pipeline at `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (the starter dependency is present, so this YAML is active \u2014 there is no `@RestController` for this path).\n\n## Gate (before anything runs)\n- **Authorization:** the whole endpoint is guarded by `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. No role \u2192 denied before step 1.\n\n## Important upfront caveat\nThe body is bound in `NormalizeAddress` with `@RequestBody` **but no `@Valid`**. So none of the JSR-380 constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`, `@Email`) are enforced. *Every* validation below is done by hand in a pipeline step. The `MethodArgumentNotValidException` / `ValidationExceptionHandler` path is effectively dead code for this endpoint.\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n**Idempotency short-circuit (first):**\n1. `CheckIdempotency` \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was already recorded (in-memory `IdempotencyStore`), branch to `RespondWithExistingOwner`, which loads the original owner and responds **200** \u2014 skipping *all* validation and side-effects below. Otherwise continue.\n\n**Validation & normalization (no transaction yet):**\n2. `NormalizeAddress` \u2014 binds body (`@RequestBody`, no `@Valid`), normalizes address fields, republishes DTO.\n3. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2192 `MissingRequiredFieldsException` **400** if firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone missing or blank (runs after normalization, so blank-after-normalize is caught; response lists the offending `fields`).\n4. `ValidateRegistrationDate` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` **400** if a supplied registration date is after today.\n5. `ValidatePostcode` \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` **400** if postcode present and not 4 digits within the city's state range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099).\n6. `NormalizeTelephone` \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` **400**; rewrites phone to E.164 (assumes +61, drops leading 0).\n7. `ValidateTelephoneLength` \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneLengthException` **400** on wrong national-number length.\n8. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` **409** if the city already has \u2265 50 owners.\n9. `NormalizeEmail` \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` **400**; lowercases + syntax-checks (optional field).\n10. `ValidateEmailDomain` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` **400** if email domain is on the blocklist.\n\n**Transaction begins here (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step from `build` to the end \u2014 commits once at the end):**\n11. `BuildOwner` \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity.\n12. `ResolveRegistrationDate` \u2014 resolves/rolls registration date to a business day.\n13. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` **429** if \u2265 100 owners already created on the resolved day.\n14. `FlagBulkSignup` \u2014 side-effect: sets bulk-signup flag if > 80 same-day signups.\n15. `FlagCapacityWarning` \u2014 side-effect: sets capacity-warning flag if city has 40\u201349 owners.\n16. `AssignMemberId` \u2014 side-effect: assigns member id.\n17. `DeduplicateMemberId` \u2014 side-effect: appends `-n` if member id collides (scans `findAll()`).\n18. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 side-effect: assigns household id.\n19. `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` **409** if SHA-256 of canonical telephone+email+Soundex(lastName) matches an active owner (bypassed when `sharesHousehold=true`; ignores soft-deleted).\n20. `CountHousehold` \u2014 side-effect: sets household size.\n21. `CapMembershipLevel` \u2014 side-effect: sets membership-level cap.\n22. `CountNamesakes` \u2014 side-effect: sets namesake count.\n23. `FlagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 side-effect: flags soft duplicate (same Soundex(lastName)+postcode, different identity) via `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.\n24. `SaveOwner` \u2014 **persists the owner** (repository `save`).\n25. `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 side-effect: records `Idempotency-Key \u2192 ownerId` in `IdempotencyStore` (first-writer-wins).\n26. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect: writes to `AUDIT` logger.\n27. `AuditOwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 side-effect: emits `OwnerCreatedEvent` (process-wide `AtomicLong` sequence) to `AUDIT`.\n28. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification` \u2014 side-effect: writes to `NOTIFY` logger.\n29. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 responds **201 Created**, `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body = `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Two structural notes\n- **Ordering matters and is deliberate:** all cheap 400-type validations run *before* the transaction opens; capacity/limit/duplicate checks (409/429) run *inside* it. A future-date or bad-postcode request is rejected without ever hitting the DB.\n- **Errors** are thrown as checked exceptions and mapped to RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` responses by escalation YAMLs under `officefloor/escalation/`; anything unmatched falls through to Spring `@RestControllerAdvice`.\n\nIf you'd like, I can flag the missing-`@Valid` gap (the DTO constraints being silently unenforced) as a potential bug rather than intended behavior."
